      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wakita%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The word Wakita is a Cherokee term for water collected in a small depression, such as a buffalo wallow.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wakita%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Wakita developed after the Hutchison and Southern Railroad built a line from southern Kansas that reached the town in February 1897.",
